# {{TITLE_TEXT}}

This is a local-first LuaLaTeX mathematics notebook based on
`qiulinfan/localLatexenv`. `main.tex` and `chapters/*.tex` are the authority.

```sh
make edit    # open the configured VS Code workspace
make pdf     # compile build/main.pdf once
make watch   # continuously rebuild build/main.pdf
make typst-preview # convert main.tex and chapters, then compile Typst preview
make typst-watch   # continuously preview the generated Typst projection
make clean   # remove local compiler output
```

LaTeX Workshop recompiles the root document on save and refreshes its internal
PDF tab; Ultra Math Preview renders the formula at the cursor. The synchronized
ElegantBook adapter writes a self-contained projection under `build/typst/`.
Use `\kn{canonical concept}` for the one authoritative graph occurrence and
`\knref{canonical concept}` elsewhere; both remain valid in the LuaLaTeX PDF
and convert to Typst graph markers.
Publishing and knowledge-graph ingestion are handled later by the repository's
multi-source export skill; this project has no direct LaTeX-to-HTML path.
